    "answer": {
      "short": "$108^\\circ$",
      "worked": "The angles of a triangle total $180^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Total parts} &= 9+2+4=15\\\\15\\text{ parts} &= 180^\\circ\\\\1\\text{ part} &= 180^\\circ\\div15=12^\\circ\\\\9\\text{ parts} &= 9\\times12^\\circ=108^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThe largest angle corresponds to 9 parts, so it is $108^\\circ$.",
